        "tree_id": "fd16695926facaac678e8fc0beb93db2cb220070",
        "message": "feat(vr): native Cardboard r7 theatre with zero-copy libmpv surface\n\nReplace the Flutter 2D stereo overlay with the real Google Cardboard SDK\npipeline, vendored from OpenNOW-VR r7.\n\nNative (android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/example/kazumi/vr):\n- Vendor all r7 VR components (renderer, session, gamepad router, menu model,\n  head pose, screen/passthrough geometry, settings store) under the app package.\n- MainActivity now hosts a plain View VrTheaterView instead of the Compose\n  VrModeHost, keeps the same Activity/FlutterEngine/media_kit Player, forces\n  landscape + immersive, and routes every key/motion/touch event to VrSession\n  so no 2D UI is reachable inside the headset.\n- VrSettingsCodec: 31 settings <-> Flutter map, single source of truth.\n- VrSession gained onEnabledChanged / onSettingsChanged callbacks so the\n  Flutter side mirrors native state both ways.\n- Re-entering VR re-installs the external-OES video texture (the EGL surface\n  survives an off/on cycle, so onSurfaceCreated does not fire again).\n\nVideo path (vendor/media_kit_video + VrSurfaceRegistry):\n- New plugin-module VrSurfaceRegistry publishes the SurfaceTexture-backed\n  Surface created by the Cardboard GL thread.\n- VideoOutput repoints libmpv --wid between the Flutter surface and the VR\n  surface, with generation tracking and delayed JNI global-ref release.\n- Lazily resolve the main Looper so pure-JVM unit tests never touch Android.\n\nFlutter:\n- VRService is now a thin facade over the native channel; no pose stream, no\n  Flutter rendering, no second settings store.\n- Deleted vr_overlay.dart / vr_gamepad.dart / vr_qr_dialog.dart.\n- New 「内容与偏好 → VR 设置」 page (also reachable from 设置 → 播放) that reads\n  and writes the same native store the in-headset GL menu edits.\n- Player keeps a native-style VR button; the decoded frame size is pushed to\n  the renderer so the theatre quad is never stretched.\n\nBuild:\n- Cardboard SDK has no Maven artifact: CI builds sdk-debug.aar from\n  third_party/cardboard, then compiles an arm64-v8a only debug APK.\n- minSdk >= 24, CAMERA permission, r7 JVM unit tests wired into CI.",
